How to use driftctl for aws terraform ?

1. driftctl is used to find differences between our AWS live infrastructure and our Terraform state files

2. driftctl needs read-only permissions to scan our AWS environment. It automatically picks up standard AWS environment variables

3.By default, running driftctl scan looks for a local terraform.tfstate file in our current working directory. 

driftctl scan --from tfstate://terraform.tfstate

4.If our AWS infrastructure is split across multiple state files, pass multiple --from flags 

driftctl scan --from tfstate+s3://my-bucket/vpc.tfstate --from tfstate+s3://my-bucket/apps.tfstate
